          "text": "The pattern is most consistently indexed by an **orthorhombic NbOF\u2083-type cell**, approximately\n\n\\[\na=13.23\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=5.41\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=4.24\\ \\text{\u00c5},\n\\]\n\nwith \\(Z=4\\). The low-angle reflections are consistent with 200, 210, 201, and an unresolved 011/400 pair. The surviving space-group assignment is **Pna2\u2081 (No. 33)**; centrosymmetric Pnma is disfavored because the observed 201 reflection violates its \\(h0l\\) condition.\n\nThe O/F assignment cannot be established reliably from Cu X-ray data because their scattering factors are almost identical. The assignment below places O on the shortest terminal Nb\u2013X site and should therefore be regarded as a chemically restrained starting model for Rietveld refinement, rather than a fully unconstrained powder solution.\n\n```cif\ndata_NbOF3_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n;Powder indexing and chemically restrained direct-space model.\n O/F ordering is not independently resolved by Cu Kalpha X-ray data.\n;\n\n_chemical_name_common                 'niobium(V) oxide trifluoride'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Nb O F3'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'NbOF3'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 4\n\n_cell_length_a                        13.234\n_cell_length_b                         5.407\n_cell_length_c                         4.238\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          303.2\n\n_space_group_crystal_system           orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P n a 21'\n_space_group_IT_number                33\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe               x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,y+1/2,z+1/2'\n3  'x+1/2,-y,z'\n4  '-x+1/2,-y+1/2,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nNb1 Nb 4 a 0.1800 0.1000 0.0000 1.0 0.006\nO1  O  4 a 0.3160 0.1000 0.0000 1.0 0.012\nF1  F  4 a 0.0350 0.1000 0.0000 1.0 0.012\nF2  F  4 a 0.1800 0.4600 0.0000 1.0 0.012\nF3  F  4 a 0.1800 0.1000 0.5000 1.0 0.012\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing supporting this cell:\n\n| Observed \\(2\\theta\\) | \\(d\\), \u00c5 | Tentative reflection |\n|---:|---:|---|\n| 13.37\u00b0 | 6.62 | 200 |\n| 21.21\u00b0 | 4.19 | 210 |\n| 24.94\u00b0 | 3.57 | 201 |\n| 26.72\u00b0 | 3.33 | 011, with nearby 400 |\n| 30.18\u00b0 | 2.96 | 211 |\n| 31.51\u00b0 | 2.84 | 410 |\n| 34.53\u00b0 | 2.60 | 401 |\n| 35.71\u00b0 | 2.51 | 220 |\n| 38.3\u201338.5\u00b0 | 2.35\u20132.34 | overlapping higher-index reflections |\n| 40.89\u00b0 | 2.21 | 600 region |\n\nThe principal surviving alternatives are not different metal frameworks but **anion-ordering variants obtained by exchanging O1 with F1, F2, or F3**. Neutron diffraction, \\(^{19}\\)F spectroscopy, or a chemically restrained Rietveld refinement would be required to select among those variants confidently.",
